# Error Handling and User-Facing Errors

- Use typed errors (enums conforming to `Error`) for domain failures; avoid bare `NSError` or stringly-typed errors at boundaries.
- Map low-level or network errors to domain errors inside the layer that owns the call; present a simple, user-friendly message (or key) in the UI.
- Document thrown errors in doc comments (`throws`, or list in `- Note:`); avoid swallowing errors without logging or rethrowing.
